Question budget)): The measured quantity is the naive estimate's bias against the selected configuration's own fresh-question accuracy (0.051 at N=60). Comparing it with the spread of pool accuracies (0.107 to 0.166) supports only that the two magnitudes are similar. No artifact measures the reported advantage over alternatives or its relation to true between-configuration differences. The measured N=60 bias is 0.051 against a spread of about 0.059. The claim is also grounded only to final.evidence.episodes.\n  - claim: so at small N the reported advantage of the selected configuration over its alternatives is as large as the differences it is meant to reveal\n  - evidence: claims_grounding.json claim \"naive optimism at N=60 (0.051) is comparable to that spread\"; source_evidence/evaluator/final_manifest.json per_config_pool_accuracy (min 0.1067, max 0.166); paper.tex Results Question budget paragraph.\n  - requested_fix: Limit the sentence to \"the optimism at N=60 is of the same order as the spread of configuration pool accuracies\", and delete or qualify the inference about the reported advantage over alternatives.\n\n## Soft warnings\n- figures[1] PNG width too small: 1650 < 2400\n- figures[2] PNG width too small: 1650 < 2400\n- figures[3] exceeds series budget in panel 0: 3 > 2\n- figures[3] PNG width too small: 1170 < 2400\nfigures:\nbias_and_coverage.pdf\nbias_and_coverage.pdf.prov.json\nbias_and_coverage.png\nbias_and_coverage.png.prov.json\noverview_schematic.png\noverview_schematic.png.prov.json\noverview_schematic.prompts.json\nper_case_interval_score.pdf\nper_case_interval_score.pdf.prov.json\nper_case_interval_score.png\nper_case_interval_score.png.prov.json\nposthoc\nwidth_vs_n.pdf\nwidth_vs_n.pdf.prov.json\nwidth_vs_n.png\nwidth_vs_n.png.prov.json\n\nscientific-evidence:\nbundle.manifest.json\nledger.jsonl\nschemas\nspec.md\nverification-report.json","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
